CSC Newsletter

CSC together with University of Helsinki and Aalto University is training two teams for the international Student Cluster Competetion (SCC) organized by the HPC-AI Advisory Council. This is the fourth time 
Finnish teams are participating the SCC and the first time there are two Finnish teams competing.
The virtual competition, to which both teams were selected, takes place in April and uses computing resources from Deutsches Klimarechenzentrum (DKRZ) and Pittsburgh Supercomputing Center (PSC).
Additionally, the CSC/UoH team will compete against 9 university teams from South Africa, Switzerland, Germany, Singapore, Taiwan, USA, China, Spain and United Kingdom in the on-site event at the 
ISC25 conference in Hamburg in June 10-12. In the on-site competition the teams work on their own mini-clusters, which for the CSC/UoH Team Lumikko will be provided by Eviden who is the vendor for CSC's 
Puhti and Mahti and the coming Roihu supercomputer. In both competitions six person student teams face various HPC related challenges like running benchmarks, reproducing results from scientific articles and trying to 
compile and run previously unknown HPC applications. CSC's goal in training and supporting the teams is to give the students an intensive and practical introduction to HPC, cluster management and working in an supercomputing 
environment and boost their studies and future careers. And an unforgettable experience of participating an international competition as a team.
